          "claim": "The existence theorem supplies the nonzero physical subspace and exact unitary evolution for the adopted finite regulator, not an assumed continuum state space.",
          "inputs": [
            "A1",
            "F1",
            "given"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "d-1.2",
          "step": "1.2",
          "claim": "Gauge invariance of a physical vector and the charge character imply expectation zero at nonzero charge; inserting gauge transformations between factors adds charges, and the cited Ward interface supplies the domain/evolution clauses.",
          "inputs": [
            "A1",
            "L1",
            "given",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "d-1.3",
          "step": "1.3",
          "claim": "The hypotheses match the domain-qualified contact interface. Between distinct insertion times the ordering is fixed; the distributional derivative is the sum of its jumps, which are the stated commutator insertions.",
          "inputs": [
            "L2",
            "given",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "d-1.4",
          "step": "1.4",
          "claim": "For the empty region both sums vanish. For any region, the Gauss identity reduces regional charge to the signed boundary electric sum; domain preservation and boundary commutation give [Q_R,O]=0, hence a nonzero fixed charge change forces O to vanish on this domain.",
          "inputs": [
            "L3",
            "given",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "d-2.1",
          "step": "2.1",
          "claim": "The support/locality premise makes O commute with E(grad chi_R); the Gauss identity gives commutation with Q_R^cont. Passing both stipulated limits yields [Q,O]=0, and the nonzero-charge equation plus boundedness and density gives O=0.",
          "inputs": [
            "L3",
            "given",
            "algebra"
          ]
        }
      ],
